BT /F1 16 Tf 40 740 Td (NEURALINK N1 BRAIN-COMPUTER INTERFACE: TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE & PRIME STUDY) Tj
0 -18 Td /F2 10 Tf (Document: NL-ENG-2026-N1-WP | Neuralink Neuroengineering, Robotic Surgery & Clinical Systems) Tj
0 -14 Td /F2 9 Tf (Classification: Technical Whitepaper | Target Device: N1 Intracortical Telemetry System) Tj
0 -20 Td /F1 11 Tf (1. Abstract & Clinical Motivation) Tj
0 -12 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (Intracortical brain-computer interfaces (BCIs) record multi-unit action potentials directly from the cerebral cortex to restore motor,) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (sensory, and digital autonomy to patients suffering from tetraplegia, severe cervical spinal cord injury (SCI, C1-C4), and amyotrophic) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (lateral sclerosis (ALS). Historical intracortical arrays (e.g., the silicon Utah microelectrode array) relied on rigid percutaneous wired pedestals) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (protruding through the cranium, posing chronic infection risks, tissue shear inflammation, and restricted mobility. The Neuralink N1 system) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (presents a fully implanted, cosmetically invisible, high-channel-count, ultra-low-power wireless BCI capable of continuous neural streaming.) Tj
0 -16 Td /F1 11 Tf (2. End-to-End System Topology) Tj
0 -12 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (The complete system architecture comprises three interconnected sub-systems: (1) The N1 Implantable Neuro-telemetry Device,) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (hermetically sealed within a cranial skull pocket; (2) The R1 Robotic Insertion System, executing autonomous stereotaxic micro-thread) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (implantation with micron-scale vascular collision avoidance; and (3) The User Terminal Processing Engine (running on iOS/macOS/Windows),) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (which performs continuous closed-loop kinematic decoding, spike sorting, and Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) encrypted handshake.) Tj
0 -16 Td /F1 11 Tf (3. Biocompatible Thin-Film Microelectrode Array Specifications) Tj
0 -12 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (The sensor array features 1024 recording microelectrodes distributed across 64 individual thin-film polyimide threads (16 sites per thread).) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (Each polyimide ribbon has a thickness of 4 to 6 micrometers, a width tapering from 50 um at the base to 5 um at the tip, and an insertion) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (depth of 3.5 to 5.0 mm into precentral motor cortex targeting Layer V large pyramidal projection neurons. The extreme mechanical flexibility) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (minimizes brain parenchymal shear strain and glial scar formation (astrogliosis), drastically extending chronical recording stability.) Tj
0 -12 Td /F2 8.5 Tf (Electrochemical Properties:) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Electrode Material: Sputtered Iridium Oxide Film (SIROF) and electrochemically deposited PEDOT:PSS conductive polymer.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- 1 kHz Electrochemical Impedance: 20 to 35 kOhms (mean: 24.8 kOhms), providing high signal-to-noise ratio (SNR > 6.8 dB).) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Charge Storage Capacity (CSC): 120 to 180 mC/cm^2, supporting safe bidirectional microstimulation up to 100 uA pulses.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Thread Spacing & Geometry: Geometric pitch of 50 to 250 um between adjacent recording sites, enabling high-density spatial sampling.) Tj
ET
endstream
