BT /F1 13 Tf 40 740 Td (4. Custom Mixed-Signal ASIC & On-Chip Neural Signal Processing) Tj
0 -18 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (At the heart of the N1 implant is a monolithic custom mixed-signal application-specific integrated circuit (ASIC) fabricated on a 28nm TSMC) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (low-power CMOS process node, measuring 4.8 mm x 4.8 mm. The ASIC integrates 1024 independent low-noise Analog Front Ends (AFEs).) Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 11 Tf (4.1. Analog Front End (AFE) Architecture & Specifications) Tj
0 -12 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Number of Channels: 1024 fully differential channels with programmable gain (40 dB to 70 dB in 6 dB increments).) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Input-Referred Noise: < 4.2 uVrms integrated over the 300 Hz to 7.5 kHz action potential recording bandwidth.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Common-Mode Rejection Ratio (CMRR): > 85 dB at 50/60 Hz and 1 kHz; Power Supply Rejection Ratio (PSRR) > 80 dB.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Power Dissipation: 5.2 uW per channel AFE; total 1024-channel analog core consumes only 5.32 mW of power.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Analog-to-Digital Conversion: 10-bit Successive Approximation Register (SAR) ADCs sampling at 20.0 kHz per channel.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (- Aggregate Raw Bandwidth: 20.48 MSamples/sec (204.8 Mbps raw uncompressed neural data output).) Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 11 Tf (4.2. On-Chip Digital Filtering & Spike Event Detection) Tj
0 -12 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (Transmitting raw 204.8 Mbps exceeds wireless BLE capacity and battery thermal limits. The digital signal processing (DSP) block computes:) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (1. Digital Bandpass Filter: 4th-order cascaded IIR filter with 300 Hz high-pass and 5 kHz low-pass cutoff frequencies.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (2. Non-Linear Energy Operator (NEO): Real-time instantaneous energy computed as psi[x(n)] = x^2(n) - x(n-1)x(n+1).) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (3. Dynamic Thresholding: Trigger threshold set to Vth = -4.5 * sigma_n, where sigma_n = median(|x(n)| / 0.6745) estimated on-chip.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (4. Spike-Band Power (SBP): Computes root-mean-square energy within 20ms bins per channel, reducing data telemetry to 200 Hz per channel.) Tj
0 -10.5 Td /F3 8.5 Tf (5. Dual Telemetry Modes: Mode A (SBP Stream at 200 kbps for continuous cursor decoding); Mode B (Raw 20 kHz Snapshot Stream for calibration).) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
